# PSR-1 — Hygiene containment proof

## Scope

| Wave | Work | Forbidden |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **PSR-1a** | Path-specific ignore for rebuildable artifacts | TEMP wipe, `git clean -fdX`, defer-docs commit |
| **PSR-1b** | Root ad-hoc / duplicate delete after consumer proof | Mixing product trains, deleting `scripts/vps-deploy/*` |

Deferred PSR-0b docs (`docs/dev/*`, `docs/phase-*`, `docs/standards/*` dirty
set) stay unstaged until PSR-2.

## PSR-1a — Ignore policy

Allowlisted rebuildable patterns reinforced in `.gitignore`:

- `.next/` (already `apps/*/.next/`)
- `dist/`, `coverage/`, `*.tsbuildinfo` (already root-wide)
- `test-results/`, `playwright-report/` (broadened beyond legacy-only)
- `.turbo/`
- `__pycache__/`, `*.pyc`
- Root ad-hoc helpers: `tmp-restart-*.mjs` (never re-commit)

**Not** ignore-targets: `node_modules` cleanup mixed into this wave, `legacy/backups`,
`legacy/logs`, `.env*`, TEMP content deletion.

## PSR-1b — Delete candidates (consumer proof)

| Candidate | Working-tree state at proof | Live consumer of **root** path | Canonical replacement | Verdict |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `bootstrap-server.sh` (root) | already deleted vs HEAD | none — CI/README use `scripts/vps-deploy/bootstrap-server.sh` | `scripts/vps-deploy/bootstrap-server.sh` | **delete from git** |
| `remote-deploy.sh` (root) | already deleted vs HEAD | none — `.github/workflows/deploy-vps.yml` calls `scripts/vps-deploy/remote-deploy.sh` | `scripts/vps-deploy/remote-deploy.sh` | **delete from git** |
| `fix-route.js` | already deleted vs HEAD | zero product/test import | n/a (one-off) | **delete from git** |
| `make-jpeg.js` | already deleted vs HEAD | zero | n/a | **delete from git** |
| `test.jpg` | already deleted vs HEAD | zero | fixtures live under package tests | **delete from git** |
| `test-proxy.js` | already deleted vs HEAD | zero | formal smoke/servers under `apps/*/scripts` | **delete from git** |
| `tmp-restart-denali-api.mjs` | untracked on disk | zero (inventory/docs only) | marketing/API smoke scripts | **rm; gitignore** |
| `tmp-restart-memory-api.mjs` | untracked on disk | zero | same | **rm; gitignore** |
| `__pycache__/*.pyc` (cursor skill) | deleted vs HEAD | rebuildable bytecode | ignore `__pycache__/` | **delete from git** |

Historical docs that mention bare `bootstrap-server.sh` / `remote-deploy.sh`
(phase-21 audits, root `PRODUCTION_RELEASE_AUDIT.md`) are shorthand for the
**vps-deploy** scripts; they are not importers of the root duplicates. Rewriting
those archives is PSR-2, not a blocker for deleting root copies.

### Proof commands (re-runnable)

```bash
# Canonical deploy still present
test -f scripts/vps-deploy/bootstrap-server.sh
test -f scripts/vps-deploy/remote-deploy.sh

# CI entrypoint is vps-deploy, not root
rg -n "scripts/vps-deploy/remote-deploy" .github/workflows/deploy-vps.yml

# No remaining root helper files on disk after PSR-1b
test ! -e bootstrap-server.sh
test ! -e remote-deploy.sh
test ! -e fix-route.js
test ! -e make-jpeg.js
test ! -e test-proxy.js
test ! -e test.jpg
test ! -e tmp-restart-denali-api.mjs
test ! -e tmp-restart-memory-api.mjs
```

